From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add LICENSE.postgresql and LICENSE.pgvector matching
 setuptools' default glob

pyproject.toml declares no license-files, so setuptools' default
LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING*/NOTICE*/AUTHORS* glob applies at the project root
only. pixeltable-pgserver's build compiles PostgreSQL 16.14 and 18.4
and the pgvector 0.8.5 extension from source (pgbuild/Makefile,
fetched at build time from ftp.postgresql.org and
github.com/pgvector/pgvector) and bundles the resulting binaries and
libraries into every wheel, but the checkout carries no license text
for either project, so neither one lands in dist-info/licenses/.

Add a copy of each project's own license text at the root as
LICENSE.postgresql (PostgreSQL's COPYRIGHT, identical for REL_16_14
and REL_18_4) and LICENSE.pgvector, which the existing default glob
already matches with no pyproject.toml change. Both are the permissive
PostgreSQL License.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against pixeltable/pixeltable-pgserver]
---
 LICENSE.pgvector   | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.postgresql | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 43 insertions(+)

